    summary: "Erdafitinib is an oral pan-FGFR (1 to 4) tyrosine kinase inhibitor for the roughly 20% of urothelial cancers with FGFR3 or FGFR2 alterations, so molecular testing is required before use. It received accelerated approval in 2019 on BLC2001 (ORR 40%) and full approval in January 2024 on THOR cohort 1, where it gave OS 12.1 versus 7.8 months (HR 0.64) against chemotherapy after platinum and immunotherapy. THOR cohort 2, against pembrolizumab in immunotherapy-naive patients, showed no benefit, so the drug is positioned after a PD-1 or PD-L1 inhibitor. Hyperphosphataemia (79%), stomatitis (58%) and central serous retinopathy (17%) need monitoring, including regular eye examinations. Johnson & Johnson develops it. It is the first targeted pill in bladder cancer, and it only works when the tumour carries the matching alteration.",
